{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_011bSMZKra9BdxkPihmiinYS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Written and committed `answers/01-017-what-is-reflection-in-the-context-of-llm-agents.md`.\n\n**What the note covers:**\n\n- **Concept:** Reflection = the generate → critique → revise self-improvement loop; the agent evaluates its own prior output and conditions the next generation on that critique\n- **Reflexion (Shinn et al., 2023):** Canonical formalization with episodic memory so the agent improves *across* tasks, not just within one run\n- **Two variants:** Introspective reflection (model critiques its own reasoning) vs tool-feedback reflection (external signal like test failure or search contradiction — more reliable)\n- **HumanEval benchmark:** 3-iteration Reflexion loop pushed GPT-4 pass@1 from ~67% → ~88%\n- **Production gotcha:** Each reflection pass ≈ 1 extra LLM call; 3 rounds = 3× token cost — recommend conditional triggering only on concrete failure signals (tool error, low confidence)\n- **Pitfalls:** Confusing \"retry\" with \"reflection\" (critique must be explicit); claiming reflection always helps without mentioning cost; not distinguishing the two reflection variants\n\nNext up: **Q18 — Explain KL divergence.**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":342,"cache_read_input_tokens":57531,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":342,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bd8210f1-60cc-4a8d-9054-ad56e8c0aace","uuid":"0bbac51f-b4fd-434f-ba06-d064f52a1a84"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":100908,"duration_api_ms":155242,"ttft_ms":6089,"ttft_stream_ms":5279,"time_to_request_ms":10,"num_turns":10,"result":"Done. Written and committed `answers/01-017-what-is-reflection-in-the-context-of-llm-agents.md`.\n\n**What the note covers:**\n\n- **Concept:** Reflection = the generate → critique → revise self-improvement loop; the agent evaluates its own prior output and conditions the next generation on that critique\n- **Reflexion (Shinn et al., 2023):** Canonical formalization with episodic memory so the agent improves *across* tasks, not just within one run\n- **Two variants:** Introspective reflection (model critiques its own reasoning) vs tool-feedback reflection (external signal like test failure or search contradiction — more reliable)\n- **HumanEval benchmark:** 3-iteration Reflexion loop pushed GPT-4 pass@1 from ~67% → ~88%\n- **Production gotcha:** Each reflection pass ≈ 1 extra LLM call; 3 rounds = 3× token cost — recommend conditional triggering only on concrete failure signals (tool error, low confidence)\n- **Pitfalls:** Confusing \"retry\" with \"reflection\" (critique must be explicit); claiming reflection always helps without mentioning cost; not distinguishing the two reflection variants\n\nNext up: **Q18 — Explain KL divergence.**","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"bd8210f1-60cc-4a8d-9054-ad56e8c0aace","total_cost_usd":0.6839992499999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":19,"cache_creation_input_tokens":106689,"cache_read_input_tokens":433355,"output_tokens":4036,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":106689},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"blackboxai/anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5":{"inputTokens":18608,"outputTokens":6539,"cacheReadInputTokens":433355,"cacheCreationInputTokens":106689,"webSearchR